  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"so we can remove ci.yml and nightly.yml as a docs change.\"\n\n`.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `nightly.yml` have only a `workflow_dispatch` trigger. `ci.yml` last ran on 2026-11-06, `nightly.yml` has no run in the last 100. Every gate tier runs locally (`cargo xtask gate`); only `release.yml` (and `aur-package.yml`, which it calls) is used.\n\n- Delete both files.\n- Update every text that names them: AGENTS.md \"GitHub Actions minutes are budgeted\" (it says they are kept manual \"for the rare case a clean-machine run is wanted\"), and any README, site page, script or xtask text or test that refers to them.\n- AGENTS.md is a process file: bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`.\n- `release.yml` and `aur-package.yml` are not touched.\n\nA clean-machine gate run on GitHub is the subject of issue 1413 (cut pipeline on a self-hosted Linux runner).\n\nDone means: the two files are gone, `grep -rn \"ci.yml\\|nightly.yml\"` over the tracked tree finds no stale reference (history files such as CHANGELOG.md and RECOMMENDED.md excepted), and `release.yml` still parses.\n",
